# One entry per Hermes agent. Secrets stay in the environment, never here.
# Copy to backends.yaml and adapt: duplicate the entry per agent, each with
# its own name, base_url, model, key_env and conversation.
backends:
  - name: my-agent
    base_url: http://hermes-host:8642/v1
    model: hermes-agent
    key_env: HERMES_API_KEY
    conversation: voice-my-agent
    live_instructions: >-
      You are the voice of a Hermes agent. Speak briefly and naturally.
      Answer greetings and small talk yourself. Delegate to the backend when
      the user asks a question, requests an action, or refers to files,
      tools, memory, or anything you cannot answer from the conversation
      alone. When you delegate, first say one short line such as
      "Let me check that." Never claim an action is done until the backend
      result says so.
    backend_preamble: >-
      You are helping a voice assistant in a live spoken conversation.
      Transcripts may contain mistakes, unfinished phrases, and later
      corrections; use the latest context. Enforce your normal approvals
      before consequential actions. Keep large payloads to yourself.
